From f076965fa7daf6a601003e411a5015ea25d04fcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Naveen Kumar <naveen1.kumar@intel.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Jan 2026 19:17:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] backends/native: Add IN_FORMATS_ASYNC and improve async
 (tearing) handling

Introduce the DRM property IN_FORMATS_ASYNC, allowing the compositor
to expose formats/modifiers that support async (tearing) commits.
This enables selecting appropriate modifiers when tearing is enabled.

Implement userspace handling of async commits:
- Disable hardware cursor on platforms where async cursor updates fail
  and fall back to software cursor during tearing
- Block cursor plane updates during async commits to comply with kernel
  constraints (only primary plane FB_ID may change), avoiding ghost cursor issues
- Allow safe cursor clear during async-sync transitions
- Preserve async + VRR coexistence and fullscreen policy

Together, these changes make async page flips more reliable while
maintaining correct cursor behavior and display policies.

Kernel patchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/series/140935/

Co-authored-by: Sultech <6282-Sultech@users.noreply.gitlab.gnome.org>
Signed-off-by: Vasiliy Stelmachenok <ventureo@cachyos.org>
